# The Listener — swamp T2 basic striker (eyeless quadruped, sound-hunter)

[title The Listener]
[image monsters/swamp_beast_3.png]
[blood #3a3024]
[stats hp=18]

* move Attack
  narration: It snaps where you are with a precision that does not need eyes.
  narration: The smooth ruin of the head tilts, finds you, and the jaws snap closed.

* move Defend
  narration: It plants four feet very still and listens harder, the head tilted off-true.

* move Recover
  narration: It pulls back into the planks, ribs flexing. Whatever it lost, the swamp returns.

* move Brutal Heavy Slow Telegraphed Attack
  narration: The shoulders bunch, the four feet plant, and it crosses the planks in two strides and is on you.

* intro
You hear yourself stop talking. Not a decision. The thing is already
coming — four-legged, pale as wet bone, the head a smooth ruin where eyes
should be. It moves toward sound the way iron moves toward a lodestone,
and you have spent the last hour speaking. Your boot creaks on the plank.
Its head snaps to you. Whatever proverb the Revathi have about silence on
the deep paths, you understand it now.

* win
+give_gold 10
+add_tag killed_the_listener
It folds onto the planks without making any sound. You wait a long
breath in case there is another one. There is not, this time. The
proverb the Revathi have about silence on the deep paths, you keep on
understanding.

* lose
It crosses the planks in two strides. The proverb the Revathi have about
silence on the deep paths, you understood too late.
